Chapter 18
Whistleblowing, bribery law, responsibility, sustainability and data ethics
الإبلاغ عن المخالفات وقوانين مكافحة الرشوة والمسؤولية والاستدامة وأخلاقيات البيانات
The last chapter of Part 2 collects the obligations a company owes outward: to the person inside it who sees something wrong, to the law that reaches its conduct abroad, to the society it operates in, to the environment it draws on, and to the people whose data it holds.
Eight outcomes meet here, which makes this the longest chapter in the book and the one most likely to supply an essay question, because every topic in it is contested, current and capable of being argued rather than recited. Take each in turn and keep the structure: what it is, what the company must do, and what the management accountant specifically contributes.
Figure F818-01 is your map.
